---
title: How to add checkbox groups in form
sidebar:
  order: 9
---
**To add phone number input support to a form, follow these steps:**

1. **Navigate to Forms Section:**
   - **Go to the “Forms” tab from the sidebar (indicated as step 1 in the second image).**
1. **Select the Form to Edit:**
   - **Select the form you want to edit from the list (indicated as step 2 in the second image).**

**To add a multiple checkbox field to your form, follow these steps:**

1. **Select “Checkbox Multiple”: On the right side of the screen, find and click the “Checkbox Multiple” option. This will add a multiple checkbox field to your form.**

**Customize the Field:**

- **Label: Set the label for the checkbox group to describe the question or prompt for the user (e.g., “What is your position?”).**
- **Required Toggle: Enable or disable the “Required” toggle based on whether you need this field to be mandatory.**
- **Add Checkbox Items: Enter the options that users can select. Each item should be a possible answer choice.**
- **Default Option (Optional): You can set a default option if needed.**

**Save the Field: Once you have configured the settings, click the “Submit” button to save the changes.**

**The multiple checkbox field will then be part of your form with all configured options.**
